 write('START-HERE.md',`# Daenem Staff Portal V3 — review checkpoint\n\n**STAFFPORTAL_SITES_REFINEMENT_INCOMPLETE**\n\nThis packet preserves the current lab, verified native image sources, available browser evidence and explicit gaps. It is not a claim of 99% quality or full contract completion.\n\nStart with MASTER-COMPLETION-REPORT.md, then known-gaps.md and feature-coverage.csv. Every retained requirement clause has a source line reference; none is automatically accepted merely because a page exists.\n\nThe ten uploaded 1672×941 dashboard mockups informed the bright white/blue composition only. They are not used as native backgrounds. Ten source photographs meet at least 3840×2160, including one verified Lagos original. Responsive variants only downsample.\n\nThe current Site work is saved without publishing. The previously published Site does not represent this checkpoint. A SOURCE-SNAPSHOT.zip is included in the external review packet.\n\nAll personal, financial and operating records are fictional. Do not enter real credentials or personal information. Production endpoint and schema unknowns retain the exact required mapping label.`);
 write('known-gaps.md',`# Open work — not a vague future roadmap\n\n${gaps.map(([id,domain,lab,expected,gap,severity])=>`## ${id} · ${domain} · ${severity}\n\nCurrent: ${lab}.\n\nMissing: ${gap}.\n\nClosure criterion: ${expected}; demonstrate the behavior and update the relevant evidence before acceptance.`).join('\n\n')}\n\nThe shared preview changed to another active project during review. No unrelated preview was stopped or modified. Final coastal text-contrast and Board & Pulse record-bucket fixes were typechecked and built, but their refreshed screenshots remain pending. Existing captures of those two screens are explicitly pre-fix evidence.`);
 write('fixture-coherence-report.md',`# Fixture coherence findings\n\nSource: model.ts seedRecords and enterprise-contract.ts enterpriseFixtures. ${records.length} fictional records are inventoried.\n\nVerified bounded invariants: approved POs contribute zero commitment; ordered/partial PO fixture commitment totals 398000 NGN; the bakery accountability example retains 16000 NGN unexplained cash variance and cannot reconcile; attendance is not Present until both accepted chronological events exist. Common home/Action Center attention uses one permitted source.\n\nA browser review found reference-identity comparisons in the Board & Pulse buckets were invalid after field projection creates new record objects. The buckets now compare stable module/id keys and exclude evidence/attention from Other active work. Final visual recapture remains pending.\n\nOpen failures: legacy finance, payroll, bakery and properties charts still use illustrative arrays; changes do not propagate through every chart, metric and related document. Receipt/PO/stock mutation is not atomic. Bakery custody is not an immutable normalized event stream. Full conservation, cross-domain lineage, duplicate import, reversal and concurrency scenarios have NOT passed.\n\nResult: PARTIAL. This report must not be presented as full fixture coherence acceptance.`);
 write('auth-flow-map.md',`# Authentication flow — fictional lab\n\nSign-in accepts a simulated Daenem account scenario and opens an assigned fictional workspace. Provisional and no-permission sessions receive an assignment-pending page with no operational navigation.\n\nRecovery proceeds from neutral account lookup to a local email-code simulation, then short-lived reset authorization, password validation and completion. The fixed preview code is displayed only within the lab. No recovery email is sent.\n\nActivation captures a fictional employee claim, verification and a new password before provisional access. Microsoft/Google show provider-configuration requirements and cannot create permissions.\n\nPassword policy: minimum 10 characters, uppercase, lowercase, number, symbol, matching confirmation and no immediate reuse. Email-code window: 2 minutes, 3 attempts, 30-second resend cooldown. Reset authorization: 5 minutes. These are simulator values, not verified Daenem production policy.\n\nRemember/trust preferences, geofence failures, network errors, locked/rate-limited accounts and temporary-password expiry are represented. Actual authentication, MFA, device trust enforcement, reset revocation, provider federation and server rate limits remain ${unknown}.`);
 write('design-system.md',`# V3 design system\n\nWhite and ice-blue surfaces, navy text, royal-blue actions, restrained violet AI/configuration accents and photographic sky/architecture headers follow the supplied post-sign-in references. Data panels remain opaque.\n\nTen sign-in compositions use separate spatial arrangements and verified native photographs. Mobile/tablet uses a compact photo followed by an accessible form. Desktop preserves composition identity; very wide screens request native originals.\n\nCanonical workspace layouts are ${m.layouts.join('; ')}. Selection follows forced organization choice, personal choice, role default and organization default. Review workbench choices do not grant permissions.\n\nTheme variables, density, motion and navigation are in portal.css and preference state. V3 additions are in auth-v3.css, enterprise-v3.css and scenery-v3.css. Builder color validation checks text/surface 4.5:1 and controls 3:1; full rendered contrast acceptance is still pending.\n\nPhotographic source credit, license and no-affiliation text are accessible from the image credit controls. Stock photography never implies an actual Daenem facility.`);
 write('component-inventory.md',`# Component inventory\n\n- Portal.tsx: route shell, session, permission gate, record mutations, dialogs and local audit.\n- lab-context.tsx: stable shared provider/hook contract. Extracted to prevent a duplicate context during module refresh.\n- model.ts / security-contract.ts: route registry, fixtures, projected fields and record scopes, capability checks and ten test profiles.\n- auth-v3.tsx / auth-contract.ts: ten compositions, form stages, password/verification rules and world clocks.\n- homes-v3.tsx / scenery-v3.tsx: ten home structures, permitted record metrics, photo headers and sidebar landscape.\n- profile-v3.tsx / attendance-v3.tsx: profile self-service and attendance event simulation.\n- table-v3.tsx: sorting, filtering, grouping, column control, views, pagination and export.\n- enterprise-v3.tsx / enterprise-contract.ts: operational ledgers, safe builder definitions, local lifecycle and domain guards.\n- workspaces.tsx / studios.tsx: retained operational pages and administration studios; review known domain-depth gaps.\n- ui.tsx and components/ui: shared controls and Radix-based dialogs, forms and disclosure primitives.\n- app/review/viewports/page.tsx: explicit CSS viewport workbench for permitted scenes.\n\nSource inventory is an implementation map, not a declaration that all components satisfy the master contract.`);
 write('offline-contract.md',`# Offline contract\n\nThe lab represents Offline, Stale, Sync Conflict and unavailable-provider states. Local records/preferences/drafts may persist in browser storage, with storage-unavailable warnings. This is not a durable production synchronization engine.\n\nRequired integration semantics: reauthorize each queued command at replay; carry an operation ID and expected revision; preserve event time separately from receipt time; reject forbidden or expired actions; surface conflicts with original and current values; deduplicate accepted work; never display a pending attendance event as accepted Present.\n\nPWA installation depends on browser support. Native background GPS, push delivery, robust install/offline behavior and operating-system certification are not implemented or proven. ${unknown}.`);
 write('accessibility-report.md',`# Accessibility evidence — incomplete\n\nImplemented: labeled authentication inputs; password visibility control; form error messages; skip link; Radix-based dialog primitives; reduced-motion CSS; theme contrast validation; clear provider-unavailable states.\n\nObserved: all ten authentication layouts have no horizontal body overflow at seven specified CSS viewports. Desktop sign-in action placement was measured within the viewport after spacing fixes. Ten Owner home layouts have no body overflow at mobile and desktop sizes. Only seven desktop home captures and eight desktop sign-in captures were preserved; the remaining captures must be repeated. These checks do not certify keyboard order, screen readers or zoom.\n\nNot completed: full keyboard traversal, visible focus under every theme, dialog traps and Escape across all flows, 200% zoom, screen-reader traversal, contrast over every crop, minimum touch targets and complete mobile navigation. Two final localized fixes need refreshed screenshots.\n\nResult: NOT ACCEPTED. Do not claim WCAG compliance or a complete accessibility pass.`);
 const totalOriginalBytes=assets.assets.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.byte_size,0),totalVariantBytes=assets.assets.reduce((n,x)=>n+x.variants.reduce((a,v)=>a+v.bytes,0),0);
 write('performance-report.md',`# Performance evidence\n\nNative sources: ${assets.assets.length} photographs, ${(totalOriginalBytes/1048576).toFixed(2)} MiB combined. Responsive WebP variants: ${(totalVariantBytes/1048576).toFixed(2)} MiB combined. These are repository totals, not initial page transfer measurements. Only the selected sign-in image is requested for its composition.\n\n640/1280/2560/3840 variants are downsampled from untouched originals. Desktop portrait crops use 3840 variants; browsers at 2200+ CSS width receive originals. That intentionally favors source fidelity and can create a large 4K transfer, especially the 13,578px Singapore image. No bandwidth, memory or decode budget has been certified.\n\nThe application uses lazy workspace loading and local table pagination. The shared context was isolated after browser QA found a refresh-related duplicate-context error; loaded desktop workspaces were rechecked successfully.\n\nNo LCP, INP, CLS, throttled mobile, route-transition percentile or large-data virtualization benchmark is reported because it was not measured. Production build success is not a performance benchmark.`);
 write('backend-implementation-notes.md',`# Backend mapping notes\n\n${unknown}. No production repository, Worker route, D1 schema, R2 bucket or external identity contract was changed or assumed.\n\nTreat api-operation-catalog.csv as semantic command/read concepts. Before integration, map each to existing production contracts and preserve verified Daenem behavior. Authorize tenant, module, record, field and specialized action on the server before metadata or bytes leave it. A client projection is not an authorization boundary.\n\nUse durable transactional semantics for PO receipt/inventory, ledger posting, payment and custody reconciliation. Validate expected revisions and operation IDs; record before/after, reason, actor, correlation and side effects. Define explicit state transitions instead of deriving permission from display order.\n\nBuilders must publish governed definitions with scope, version, validation, simulation, approval, rollback and an actual runtime consumer. Their present local UI does not provide that complete engine.\n\nInvestigate existing schema and services before classifying a gap as new capability or new migration. No production migration is included.`);
 write('database-mapping-notes.md',`# Database mapping boundary\n\n${unknown}. domain-entity-catalog.csv contains ${entities.length} logical concepts and relationship/query/retention needs. It is not a discovered database schema.\n\nRecordData is a lab display envelope with string-valued fields. Do not migrate that envelope wholesale into production tables. Map typed money, quantities, identifiers, dates, revisions and immutable events to existing normalized domain entities.\n\nCompany scope must be carried and enforced in every query. Review indexes for tenant/scope, opaque ID, event time, state and assignment expiry against actual production workloads. Establish retention and evidence/audit linkage by domain.\n\nNo table name, index, D1 migration, SQL statement or production schema change is asserted or authored. Migration risk remains unknown until read-only backend inspection.`);
 write('frontend-transfer-notes.md',`# Frontend transfer notes\n\nContinue the existing React/Vinext lab; preserve valid prior components. Route registry and authorization live in model.ts. Portal owns local session/record state and delegates to lazy Workspace; lab-context.tsx keeps the provider identity separate from the refreshable route component.\n\nCopy approved page structures and semantic tokens only after requirement-level review. Replace browser-local fixtures and audit with mapped authoritative adapters. Preserve neutral unavailable behavior and permission-filtered search, navigation, fields, counts, AI context and exports.\n\nRe-use shared Radix controls and source styles; do not reverse-engineer screenshots. Fonts and prior source credits remain under docs. All ten image sources and variants are in public/assets/scenery with provenance in image-assets.json.\n\nReview workbench is QA-only. Existing published Site is an earlier revision because this checkpoint is not deployed. GitHub transfer is not authorized and not performed.\n\nOpen transfer gates: domain coherence, full authentication and attendance policies, durable files and audit, runtime configuration, full 182-case priority matrix, accessibility and measured performance.`);
 write('handoff-notes.md',`# Handoff boundary\n\nThe user explicitly requested continuation of the existing Sites project and prohibited production deployment, GitHub writes and production Cloudflare/D1/R2 changes. This checkpoint is saved without deployment. The existing published URL remains the prior publication and must not be described as the updated preview.\n\nThe internal browser preview is a testing tool, not a user deliverable. A shared preview switch interrupted remaining tests; an unrelated project was not stopped. Use the saved source and evidence to resume review.\n\nNo independent 99% score is asserted. The correct status is STAFFPORTAL_SITES_REFINEMENT_INCOMPLETE. Continue from known-gaps.md and the source-line requirement ledger.`);
 const zeroCount=checks.results.filter(r=>/authorized projection|surface contains|scope|assignment|override|Secret fields|hidden field|current identity|export is not inferred|Company scopes/.test(r.name)).length;
 write('MASTER-COMPLETION-REPORT.md',`# Master checkpoint report\n\n**STAFFPORTAL_SITES_REFINEMENT_INCOMPLETE**\n\nThe imagery and layout refinement is implemented in the existing lab. The complete master contract is not independently proven and several substantive workflows remain partial. This report records an honest checkpoint, not a completed enterprise product.\n\n## Current implementation\n\nTen distinct sign-in compositions now use verified native 4K-or-larger originals. Nine international settings complement one native 6637×4425 Lagos photo. The uploaded dashboard mockups were excluded from runtime imagery because they are 1672×941 interface references. Ten post-sign-in structures use bright architectural/landscape headers and opaque operational panels.\n\nThe continued lab adds profile and attendance experiences, expanded permissions and projections, new procurement/custody workspaces, local versioned builders, saved views, table controls and richer source-derived metrics. See known-gaps.md for their concrete limitations.\n\n## Required handoff fields\n\n| Field | Evidence / status |\n|---|---|\n| SITES_BUILD_STATUS | Validated build recorded separately; saved checkpoint without deployment |\n| PRIVATE INTERACTIVE PREVIEW | No newly published preview; existing publication is older. Internal review is not a handoff URL. |\n| TOTAL ROUTES | ${m.modules.length} registered primary workspace routes plus sign-in, review utilities and dynamic record paths |\n| TOTAL PRIMARY WORKSPACES | ${m.modules.length} module definitions; not ${m.modules.length} complete domain workflows |\n| TOTAL FEATURES | Not independently tallied; ${requirements.length} source-clause rows retained for granular acceptance |\n| TOTAL INTERACTIVE FEATURES | Not independently tallied; do not equate route controls with complete features |\n| TOTAL VERIFIED FEATURE REQUIREMENTS | No independent full requirement acceptance count established |\n| TOTAL ZERO-DISCLOSURE TESTS | ${zeroCount} bounded deterministic authorization/projection checks in the source suite |\n| ZERO-DISCLOSURE TEST RESULT | PASS for the bounded source checks; BLOCKED/NOT COMPLETE for end-to-end product and production certification |\n| TOTAL BUSINESS RULES | ${b.businessRules.length} cataloged invariants; enforcement depth varies |\n| TOTAL WORKFLOW STATE MACHINES | ${m.modules.length} registered state lists; complete guarded graphs not established |\n| TOTAL API OPERATIONS IDENTIFIED | ${operations.length} semantic mapping candidates; no production endpoint claimed |\n| TOTAL DATA ENTITIES IDENTIFIED | ${entities.length} logical concepts; no production schema claimed |\n| TOTAL PRODUCTION BACKEND GAPS | ${gaps.length} grouped gap areas; current contracts unknown |\n| TOTAL VISUAL QA SCREENS | Preserved: 8 desktop sign-in captures, 7 desktop Owner home captures, 2 4K sign-in captures; 10 variants of each were measured |\n| VIEWPORT MATRIX | Auth: 70 width measurements. Owner layouts: 20 mobile/desktop width measurements. Required priority matrix: 26×7, incomplete. |\n| ACCESSIBILITY | Partial implementation; full keyboard/zoom/contrast/touch certification pending |\n| PERFORMANCE | Asset byte/dimension evidence; no fabricated load or interaction metrics |\n| NATIVE 4K SIGN-IN ASSETS | 10 out of 10 source originals verified |\n| KNOWN GAPS | known-gaps.md and production-gap-map.csv |\n| CRITICAL BLOCKERS | Production authorization/identity mapping, transactional coherence, domain depth, files/audit, complete browser acceptance |\n| READY FOR BACKEND MAPPING | YES as a clearly incomplete discovery input; NO as a finalized integration specification |\n| READY FOR GITHUB FRONTEND TRANSFER | NO |\n| READY FOR STAGING INTEGRATION | NO |\n| READY FOR PRODUCTION | NO |\n| READY FOR INDEPENDENT CHATGPT REVIEW | YES for this checkpoint; NO for complete-product acceptance |\n\n## Verification\n\nDeterministic fictional-source suite: ${checks.passed}/${checks.total} checks passed. This does not establish whole-product security. Native original hashes/dimensions and responsive variant sizes are recorded. Browser QA exposed and fixed a duplicated React context during refresh; all ten loaded desktop home layouts were then rechecked. The final coastal text-background correction and stable-key Board & Pulse bucket fix require fresh captures when the shared preview is available.\n\n## Protected boundaries\n\nGITHUB MODIFIED: NO\n\nPRODUCTION CLOUDFLARE MODIFIED: NO\n\nPRODUCTION D1 WRITTEN: NO\n\nPRODUCTION R2 WRITTEN: NO\n\nPRODUCTION DEPLOYED: NO\n\nSaving the lab source to its existing Sites repository is not a GitHub write or a production deployment.`);
 write('handoff-counts.json',JSON.stringify({generatedAt:new Date().toISOString(),status:'STAFFPORTAL_SITES_REFINEMENT_INCOMPLETE',modules:m.modules.length,requirementSourceClauses:requirements.length,sourceChecks:checks.total,sourceChecksPassed:checks.passed,boundedAuthorizationChecks:zeroCount,logicalEntities:entities.length,semanticOperations:operations.length,businessRules:b.businessRules.length,gapAreas:gaps.length,authMeasurements:evidence.auth.length,homeMeasurements:evidence.homes.length,native4kOriginals:assets.assets.length,independentAcceptance:false},null,2));
 console.log(JSON.stringify({files:fs.readdirSync(out).length,modules:m.modules.length,sourceClauses:requirements.length,entities:entities.length,operations:operations.length},null,2));
